# Text files are stored and checked out with LF on every OS, so shell scripts run under Git Bash and WSL, fixtures and
# test expectations are byte-identical, and lock files never churn. Windows batch files need CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
# Binary assets
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.zip binary
*.wasm binary
*.ttf binary
*.woff2 binary
